0001:    REM \u8216?C64FX - Commodore 64 sound tricks on the C47 buzzer (one voice)\u8217?\par
0002:    REM \u8216?The C64's SID chip had 3 voices, 4 waveforms, ADSR envelopes and a filter.\u8217?\par
0003:    REM \u8216?The C47 has ONE buzzer that plays one square-ish note at a time. C64\u8217?\par
0004:    REM \u8216?musicians used three tricks to sound richer than the hardware; this demo\u8217?\par
0005:    REM \u8216?plays all three, in A minor (an original tune, about 15 s):\u8217?\par
0006:    REM \u8216?1. Fake chords (arpeggio): the three notes of a chord in turn, 30 ms\u8217?\par
0007:    REM \u8216?each, so fast that the ear hears one chord.\u8217?\par
0008:    REM \u8216?2. Vibrato: one long note cut into 25 ms pieces whose pitch goes up and\u8217?\par
0009:    REM \u8216?down 1.2 % along a sine (about 6.7 times a second).\u8217?\par
0010:    REM \u8216?3. Envelope: one note cut into 5 pieces of 40 ms at volume 11 8 6 4 2,\u8217?\par
0011:    REM \u8216?so it sounds plucked (loud attack, fading tail).\u8217?\par
0012:    REM \u8216?Sound commands (C47 firmware, c47-dmcp/hal/audio.c):\u8217?\par
0013:    REM \u8216?BUZZ   Y = frequency in Hz (whole Hz, 0 = silence), X = length in ms\u8217?\par
0014:    REM \u8216?(max 2000); the program waits until the note ends. Stack unchanged.\u8217?\par
0015:    REM \u8216?VOL n  buzzer volume 0-11;  VOL# puts the current volume in X;\u8217?\par
0016:    REM \u8216?VOL IND "KVOL" sets it from a variable (used to give yours back).\u8217?\par
0017:    REM \u8216?TONE n / BEEP play fixed 250 ms notes (not used here).\u8217?\par
0018:    REM \u8216?The PC simulator plays TONE and BEEP only: BUZZ and PLAY are silent there,\u8217?\par
0019:    REM \u8216?so run C64FX on the calculator.\u8217?\par
0020:    REM \u8216?Notes are given as semitones from A4 (440 Hz): 0 = A4, 3 = C5, 7 = E5,\u8217?\par
0021:    REM \u8216?-4 = F4 ...  LBL 05 turns them into Hz: f = 440 x 2^(s/12).\u8217?\par
0022:    REM \u8216?Uses: local registers only (LocR), variable KVOL (deleted at the end).\u8217?\par
0023:    REM \u8216?Side effect: the angle mode is set to DEG (for the vibrato's SIN).\u8217?\par
0024:    REM \u8216?---- main: the three parts in turn, then your volume back\u8217?\par
\par
0025:    LBL \u8216?C64FX\u8217?\par
0026:    VOL#\par
0027:    STO \u8216?KVOL\u8217?\par
0028:    DEG\par
